---
description: Avoid insecure cryptographic practices and use strong encryption
alwaysApply: true
---

insecure-crypto:

- Never use weak or deprecated cryptographic algorithms (MD5, SHA1, DES, RC4)
- Use strong algorithms: AES-256-GCM, SHA-256, bcrypt, scrypt, or Argon2
- Use cryptographically secure random number generators
- Never implement custom cryptography
- Use TLS 1.2 or higher for network communications
- Store passwords using proper hashing with salt

Weak patterns to avoid:
```javascript
crypto.createHash('md5').update(password).digest('hex');
crypto.createCipher('des', key);
Math.random() for security tokens;
```

Strong patterns to use:
```javascript
bcrypt.hash(password, 10);
crypto.createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', key, iv);
crypto.randomBytes(32);
```
